        {
          "name": "sequentialOutput",
          "type": "Boolean!",
          "description": "Sequential output refers to the sequencing of the work order processes within a given work order process group.\n\nWhen True - all work order processes will be completed finish to start. Logic: Sum of all work order process durations = Group duration.\n\nWhen False - the group will be completed in parallel: Logic:\nLongest running work order process duration = Group duration.\n\nDefault = True",
          "metadata": {
            "mfgx": {
              "mutations": {
                "create": {
                  "include": true
                },
                "update": {
                  "include": true
                }
              },
              "queries": {
                "include": true
              },
              "where": {
                "include": true
              },
              "defaultValue": true
            },
            "unique": false
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "singleSetupDuration",
          "type": "Boolean!",
          "description": "When True (managed by user at time of creating the group) - then aggregate (average) all the setupRates of all associated work Order Processes within the group.\n\nuse the setupRate field, to indicate the \"true\" initial setup time for the entire group.\n\nDefault = False",
          "metadata": {
            "mfgx": {
              "mutations": {
                "create": {
                  "include": true
                },
                "update": {
                  "include": true
                }
              },
              "queries": {
                "include": true
              },
              "where": {
                "include": true
              },
              "defaultValue": false
            },
            "unique": false
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "useMinorSetupDuration",
          "type": "Boolean!",
          "description": "Minor Setup durations - are additional / incremental setup durations required between work order processes -\n\nONLY applies - when sequentialOutput = True \nAND\nwhen the timeToStart field on the WorkOrderProcess is > 0 (seconds)\n\nWhen these conditions are met - the Schedule Output - needs to include the total of all the timeToStart durations as \"additionalSetupDuration\" to provide the accurate 'overall run time' for the work order process group. \n\nWhen updating / creating Work Order Process distributions - for each work order process within the Group - the start/end and durations of those individual distributions must incorporate the value from the timeToStart field. This value maybe unique for each work order process within the group.",
          "metadata": {
            "mfgx": {
              "mutations": {
                "create": {
                  "include": true
                },
                "update": {
                  "include": true
                }
              },
              "queries": {
                "include": true
              },
              "where": {
                "include": true
              },
              "defaultValue": false
            },
            "unique": false
          }
        },
